    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Description\n\nI noticed that mini.jump2d adds jump spots to the mini.map window:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba59b995-2f1f-49b4-abe4-aaad2dcf9f5f)\n\nAfter looking at the code, it seems it would be quite straightforward to allow for a window_filter function in the `allowed_windows` config section.\nIf a function was defined there, it could be called in the current filter (lines 820-822) after the current check for current/not_current and check for custom conditions like `filetype != 'minimap`.\n\nIf this is a good idea, I can try to provide a PR (bearing in mind that I am very new to neovim...)\n\nThanks for your great work!\n",
