    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThere is a planned substantial makeover of 'mini.jump2d' (#1818), after which this particular problem of jump spots appearing in 'mini.map' window should not be a problem (as jumping would require pressing at least one extra key to define jump spots; like `k` to jump to letter `k`, for example).\n\nHowever, jump spots appearing in 'mini.map' window in particular is more or less useful *if* the window itself is focusable (which is controlled by `MiniMap.config.window.focusable`, which is `false` by default). I think limiting 'mini.jump2d' to only consider focusable windows is a better approach here. I'll take a look.",
